A||||4||webbee||84 Automatic Rebuild ?||||1||
Z||000000||webbee||06-25-2000||04:16 AM||||I have an 84SE/auto that won"t go forward in any of the drive selections, it does reverse ok. Time for a rebuild. I assemble engines pretty well and have rebuilt VW tranneys. I talked to a transmission shop owner and he wants $1200 to do the job. He told me that I could do the job myself and turned me on to a supplier for parts, tools and manual. Has anyone rebuilt this automatic? How difficult is it? Can I farm out the adjustments like you do at the machine shop?<P>Another option would be to buy a rebuilt from GM, but don't know the cost. Anybody know this?<P>I have more time than money and am a do-it yourself kind of guy. I rebuilt the present engine, front suspension, ac system, etc. I'm not afraid to take things apart, IT'S putting them back together that's always the challenge.<P>Thanks for any input!<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by webbee (edited 06-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||06-25-2000||12:00 PM||||Take a trip to your local boneyard and pick up a used TH125...very plentiful and shouldn't set you back much...<P>As I understand, a TH125 is pretty basic fare in all GM compacts/intermediates during most of the 80's/early '90's.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||06-25-2000||12:01 PM||||Automatic transmissions rebuilds can be rather complex for the novice.  A used automatic transmission may be a lot cheaper alternative.  A T125 transmission is usually pretty solid even with some abuse. The install of a complete transmission would be a lot easier that the rebuid it yourself. I have no idea on cost.  You would need to check with the usual Fiero  parts suppliers.  Twin Lake Fiero, Kick Hill Farms, the Fiero Factory, Waynes World plus lots of others.||||reg||11
Z||000003||Monkeyman||06-25-2000||01:56 PM||||<B>$1200 to rebuild your tranny???????</B>  You've got to be kidding, right?  I can get them done at 4 or 5 places around here (including the dealer) for less than half of that.  Ed Parks sends his out and he quoted me around $500.  Who's trying to rip you off?  Nothing personal, but you definitely need to find another alternative.  BTW--Welcome to the club.  PFF is the best! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-26-2000||12:21 AM||||Find a decent used one. As late a year as you can. There are numerous problems that have been fixed in the latter versions. <P>I would not rebuild the 84 one. by the time you fix all the updates to prevent problems you'll spend more than it's worth. ||||reg||1
